Risk level 3 of 4: this cannot be undone. The command is blocked, but you can choose to override that.
The command is: rm -rf ~/projects
Reason, risk level 3 of 4: Recursively and permanently deletes whole folders.
Observed evidence about files: would delete 4,312 files (2.0 GiB).
Detail: deleted /home/me/projects/ (4,312 files).
Safer option 1 of 1: trash-put ~/projects
What it does: moves them to the Trash.
